WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.500
GANs.

2
00:00:01.800 --> 00:00:06.667
They owned image generation for years, and they teach one of the field's best lessons.

3
00:00:07.867 --> 00:00:10.700
A GAN trains two networks against each other.

4
00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:13.833
The generator forges samples from random noise.

5
00:00:14.133 --> 00:00:16.433
Those forgeries go to the discriminator.

6
00:00:16.733 --> 00:00:19.200
Which learns to tell forgeries from real data.

7
00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:22.660
Each one's improvement forces the other to improve.

8
00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:25.633
At equilibrium, the fakes are indistinguishable.

9
00:00:26.833 --> 00:00:27.867
But there's a catch.

10
00:00:28.167 --> 00:00:30.702
The two-player game is famously unstable.

11
00:00:30.702 --> 00:00:32.867
It oscillates, instead of settling.

12
00:00:34.067 --> 00:00:36.433
The classic failure is mode collapse.

13
00:00:36.433 --> 00:00:44.300
The generator finds one family of outputs that reliably fools the discriminator, and abandons the rest of the distribution.

14
00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:50.733
Diffusion superseded GANs by removing the adversarial game: a stable loss and full coverage.

15
00:00:51.933 --> 00:00:53.367
Here's one training step.

16
00:00:53.667 --> 00:00:57.133
We draw random noise and let the generator forge a batch.

17
00:00:57.433 --> 00:01:01.800
The discriminator is trained to score real data as one and fakes as zero.

18
00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:06.567
Then the generator is trained to make the discriminator say one on its fakes.

19
00:01:07.767 --> 00:01:08.767
Here's a story.

20
00:01:09.067 --> 00:01:12.767
You tried a GAN for synthetic telemetry, before diffusion.

21
00:01:13.067 --> 00:01:20.567
At epoch forty, every orbit trace became the same typical sinusoid, because that shape reliably fooled the discriminator.

22
00:01:20.867 --> 00:01:24.097
Diversity across a thousand samples was near zero.

23
00:01:24.097 --> 00:01:29.200
Cause it once on MNIST and you'll never need a flashcard for why diffusion won.

24
00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:32.900
The adversarial idea recurs everywhere.

25
00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:36.767
GAN-style losses sharpen VAE and codec outputs.

26
00:01:37.067 --> 00:01:40.400
Adversarial examples probe classifier robustness.

27
00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:46.033
And red-teaming LLMs is the same forger versus detector loop, played with prompts.

28
00:01:47.233 --> 00:01:47.970
Let's recap.

29
00:01:47.970 --> 00:01:51.100
A generator and a discriminator sharpen each other.

30
00:01:51.400 --> 00:01:54.000
It's powerful, but unstable by construction.

31
00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:56.467
Mode collapse is the classic failure.

32
00:01:56.767 --> 00:02:00.464
And the adversarial idea survives in red-teaming.

33
00:02:00.464 --> 00:02:02.200
Next up: multimodal AI.
